 ('ENT_DEMX_ROSIER','PER_EARLY_MODERN_OCCULT','Demon of carnal love/seduction in Michaelis'' Admirable History (1612), of the third hierarchy (Dominions), opposed by St. Basil. Attested essentially only in Michaelis.'),
 ('ENT_DEMX_BAALBERITH','PER_EARLY_MODERN_OCCULT','In Michaelis'' Admirable History (1612) the demon of blasphemy/quarrels, of the second hierarchy (Cherubim), opposed by St. Barnabas; later catalogues (de Plancy) make him the secretary/keeper of the archives of Hell. Derived from the biblical Baal-berith of Judges 8-9. HOMONYM: distinct from the existing Goetic spirit ENT_GOE_BERITH (Berith/Bolfry of the Ars Goetia), with which the name overlaps.'),
 ('ENT_DEMX_TITIVILLUS','PER_EARLY_MODERN_OCCULT','The medieval-to-early-modern patron demon of scribes'' errors who collects mangled and skipped words from copyists and careless reciters of the Divine Office into a sack to be read against them at Judgment; attested from John of Wales / the Tractatus de Penitentia and later sermon and exemplum literature, surviving into early-modern demonology compendia.'),
 ('ENT_DEMX_WITCH_FAMILIAR','PER_EARLY_MODERN_OCCULT','Class hub for the low demonic attendant spirits (''imps''/familiars) in animal form (cat, toad, dog, etc.) said in early-modern English and continental witch-trial demonology (e.g. the Essex trials, Matthew Hopkins'' Discovery of Witches, 1647) to be given by the Devil to suckle on the witch''s mark and do her bidding. A class, not a single named being.');
INSERT INTO entity_periods (entity_id,period_id,confidence,rationale,source_id,review_status)
INSERT INTO _r VALUES
 ('ENT_CHR_LUCIFER','member_of','ENT_GOE_SEVEN_DEADLY_DEMONS','high','Binsfeld assigns Lucifer the sin of pride among the seven princes; wired to the EXISTING Binsfeld collective (ENT_DEMX_SEVEN_PRINCES dropped as a duplicate of it).'),
 ('ENT_CHR_LUCIFER','embodies','ENT_PRIDE','high','In the Binsfeld deadly-sin schema Lucifer is the demon of pride (superbia); ENT_PRIDE is a moral abstraction, not a deity.'),
 ('ENT_CHR_MAMMON','member_of','ENT_GOE_SEVEN_DEADLY_DEMONS','high','Binsfeld assigns Mammon the sin of greed/avarice among the seven princes.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_ASMODEUS','member_of','ENT_GOE_SEVEN_DEADLY_DEMONS','high','Binsfeld assigns Asmodeus the sin of lust; existing Second-Temple Asmodeus is the figure received into this schema.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_SATAN','member_of','ENT_GOE_SEVEN_DEADLY_DEMONS','medium','Binsfeld assigns Satan the sin of wrath; wired to the existing Satan entity rather than creating a duplicate.'),
 ('ENT_CHR_BEELZEBUL','member_of','ENT_GOE_SEVEN_DEADLY_DEMONS','high','Binsfeld assigns Beelzebub the sin of gluttony; wired to the existing Beelzebul entity (homonym of ENT_LAT_BEELZEBOUL).'),
 ('ENT_CHR_LEVIATHAN','member_of','ENT_GOE_SEVEN_DEADLY_DEMONS','high','Binsfeld assigns Leviathan the sin of envy; wired to the existing Christian/Biblical Leviathan.'),
 ('ENT_GOE_BELPHEGOR','member_of','ENT_GOE_SEVEN_DEADLY_DEMONS','high','Binsfeld assigns Belphegor the sin of sloth; wired to the existing Goetic Belphegor.'),
 ('ENT_DEMX_VERRINE','member_of','ENT_DEMX_LOUDUN','high','Verrine is one of the named possessing demons enumerated in Michaelis'' Admirable History.'),
 ('ENT_DEMX_GRESIL','member_of','ENT_DEMX_LOUDUN','high','Gresil is one of the named possessing demons enumerated in Michaelis'' Admirable History.'),
 ('ENT_DEMX_SONNEILLON','member_of','ENT_DEMX_LOUDUN','high','Sonneillon is one of the named possessing demons enumerated in Michaelis'' Admirable History.'),
 ('ENT_DEMX_CARREAU','member_of','ENT_DEMX_LOUDUN','high','Carreau is one of the named possessing demons enumerated in Michaelis'' Admirable History.'),
 ('ENT_DEMX_CARNIVEAN','member_of','ENT_DEMX_LOUDUN','high','Carnivean is one of the named possessing demons enumerated in Michaelis'' Admirable History.'),
 ('ENT_DEMX_OEILLET','member_of','ENT_DEMX_LOUDUN','high','Oeillet is one of the named possessing demons enumerated in Michaelis'' Admirable History.'),
 ('ENT_DEMX_ROSIER','member_of','ENT_DEMX_LOUDUN','high','Rosier is one of the named possessing demons enumerated in Michaelis'' Admirable History.'),
 ('ENT_DEMX_BAALBERITH','member_of','ENT_DEMX_LOUDUN','high','Baalberith (Balberith) is enumerated among the possessing/expelled demons in Michaelis'' Admirable History.'),
 ('ENT_DEMX_BAALBERITH','aligned_with','ENT_GOE_BERITH','medium','The Michaelis/de Plancy Baalberith overlaps in name and demonic identity with the Goetic spirit Berith (Baal-berith of Judges); marked as a modern/functional alignment, noting the homonym, not a strict equation.'),
 ('ENT_DEMX_TITIVILLUS','member_of','ENT_DEMX_WITCH_FAMILIAR','low','Provisional placement of Titivillus among the lesser/menial demonic agents class; a minor functional demon (collector of scribal errors) rather than a prince, grouped with the low-demon class hub for connectivity.'),
 ('ENT_DEMX_TITIVILLUS','member_of','ENT_CHR_LUCIFER','low','As a lesser fallen spirit in the Christian demonological scheme, Titivillus serves under the chief of the fallen angels; a soft subordination/membership edge to Lucifer for graph connectivity (recast from the original reception_of, which denotes tradition-reception not hierarchy).'),
 ('ENT_DEMX_WITCH_FAMILIAR','member_of','ENT_ISR_SATAN','medium','Witch-trial demonology holds familiar spirits are imps assigned by the Devil to the witch under the demonic pact; the class is subordinate to / derives under Satan (recast from reception_of to member_of for correct subordination semantics).');
